{
 "about": "The judged set of P22 Milestone 6 (ADR 0173): the letters of the letter fault bench (emb_cli::letter_faults, 25 mm, default satin settings) of the four fonts with a source font in the program, as the embroidery font (emb) and as lettering in the source font (ttf). Judged by Claude on 2026-11-25 from pictures with no marks of the measures (python tools/letter-faults.py <faults.json> <out.png> --plain): the area of the outline, the stitches as thread 0.3 mm wide and the edge of the outline. The owner looked at 50 of them on 2026-11-25 (all the faulty letters, the letters near a limit, the letters that the measures of the bench call faulty, and some at random) and saw them in the same way: no corrections.",
 "rule": "A letter has a fault where the eye sees it on a sew-out of 25 mm: fabric that shows in one patch of about 0.5 mm2 or more (open-area; thin slivers between the stitches of a curve close when the thread spreads), a corner of the outline that the stitches clip (open-corner), thread clearly out of the outline (spike), a column clearly wider than its stroke (bulge), stitches that cross in a pile (crossing). A column on top of another does not show in a flat picture and is not judged. Faults: clean, open-area, open-corner, spike, bulge, crossing.",
